It’s rare for a tropical cyclone to occur in Arizona, but there’s a high risk of flash floods starting early next week, as Hurricane Rosa’s residual energy crosses the Southwest Desert.
On Monday and Tuesday, the National Bureau of Meteorology issued flashwater warnings from western Arizona, including Phoenix, Flagstaff, Las Vegas, and Salt Lake City, to southern and eastern Nevada, southeastern California and Utah.
Rosa is expected to approach late Monday, accompanied by rainfall, with a direct hit to Phoenix on Tuesday.
