"Total rainfall from three to six inches, up to 10 inches is expected from Baja California to northwest Sonora," weather.com reported.
Rosa will move northward across Mexico as a tropical cyclone as a tropical cyclone in the early hours of Tuesday morning, across Mexico as a tropical storm, as well as passing through Arizona by midnight on Tuesday into southern Utah.
"Rosa, and the main danger that will have its effects, is a very large amount of precipitation in Baja California, north-west Sonora, and in the United States," the national hurricane center said.
