Then you have to test your love.”
There were at least two boozes from the audience in his comments, and SNL's performers seemed puzzled, Variety reported that one of them said: "The whole studio was quiet."
West was invited as a replacement for singer Ariana Grande, whose former rapper Mac Miller died a few days earlier.
West, dressed as a Perrier bottle, sang "I Love It," bewildered a lot of people.
Candace Turner, the leader of the conservation group TPUSA, tweeted in support of West: "To the most brave spirit: Thank you for confronting the rioters."
However, talk show host Karen Hunter tweeted that West was simply "like them and a very great thing."
"Even I chose not to reward anyone (by buying his music and clothing, by supporting his "art") to spread an ideology that is harmful to my community.
He's free.
It's us, too," she added.
Prior to the show, the rapper announced on Twitter that he had changed his name, saying he is now "officially known as Kanye West."
He's not the first artist to change his name, and he's following in the footsteps of Diddy, also known as Paphudadi, Paffy and P Diddy.
His fellow rapper Snoop Dogg also had the name Snoop Lion, and of course the musical legend, the late Prince, changed his name to the symbol and then changed his name to "an artist formerly known as Prince."
Charged with attempted stabbing to death at a restaurant in Belfast
