But polls released on Thursday showed that a majority of Warren's own constituencies don't think she's going to run for 2020.
Fifty-eight percent of "high-potential" Massachusetts voters said senators shouldn't run, according to Suffolk University's Center for Political Research/Boston Globe polls.
Thirty-two percent supported their candidacy.
Opinion polls showed that more people supported the candidacy of former governor Deval Patrick, and 38 percent supported the possibility of a candidacy, with 48 per cent opposed.
The names of other high-profile Democratic politicians who are being debated on the possibility of a candidacy in 2020 include former Vice President Joe Biden and Vermont Senator Bernie Sanders.
